    <section>
        <h2>Introduction</h2>
        <p>
            C++ is a general-purpose, high-performance programming language.  
            It is an extension of C language that supports Object-Oriented Programming.  
            C++ is widely used in developing system software, game engines, real-time simulations, and large-scale applications.
        </p>

        <h2>Key Features of C++</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Object-Oriented:</b> Supports classes, objects, inheritance, polymorphism, and encapsulation.</li>
            <li><b>High Performance:</b> Closer to hardware, faster execution compared to many high-level languages.</li>
            <li><b>Portable:</b> Programs can run on different platforms with minimal changes.</li>
            <li><b>Standard Template Library (STL):</b> Provides powerful data structures and algorithms.</li>
            <li><b>Memory Control:</b> Provides low-level memory manipulation using pointers.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Applications of C++</h2>
        <p>C++ is used in a wide range of fields:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Game development (Unreal Engine is built in C++).</li>
            <li>Operating Systems (Windows, Linux components).</li>
            <li>Compilers & Interpreters.</li>
            <li>High-performance applications like Database Systems.</li>
            <li>Embedded systems and real-time simulations.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Why Learn C++?</h2>
        <p>
            Learning C++ helps in understanding the core concepts of programming and system-level design.  
            It is considered one of the most powerful languages for solving complex problems and is still in demand in competitive programming and software development.
        </p>
